// From delegated-task.json. The state of one child task of a delegation batch, carried whole on
// every delegated_task event (each transition is a fresh snapshot). Read from DelegatedTask
// (web/src/assistant/delegationContract.ts, validDelegatedTask;
// packages/harness/delegationContract.ts in this harness). Open: validDelegatedTask accepts a
// member it does not name. The model asks for a batch with the host tool delegate_tasks. In this
// harness (agent#14) the call runs the batch: an engine that awaits a tool call (vercel) gets the
// children's findings as that call's result ($defs/answer) in the same run; an engine whose run
// cannot wait for one (codex: the provider account runs one agent run at a time and the children
// need it) emits delegation_requested and ends its run, and the coordinator
// (packages/harness/delegation.ts, withDelegation) runs the batch and starts the response's next
// run with the call's result and nothing else. The coordinator runs the children on the same
// engine and emits these events. Its shared limits: the response's model requests (one kept for
// the parent), MAX_TOOLS tool calls (20) across the parent and its children, the turn's test
// calls, at most four batches (MAX_BATCHES) and, on an agent capability, five agent runs; each
// child's own are its profile's budget ($defs/profile, $defs/budget), which replace the Desk's
// MAX_CHILD_MODELS, MAX_CHILD_TOOLS and CHILD_TIMEOUT (budget.json $defs/deskLimits). The members
// after failure are this harness's (agent#13, agent#14, agent#15, agent#16, agent#17, agent#18).
// What a child returns (agent#16): its report ($defs/report, in its profile's shape) beside its
// text; what its run asked of the parent (a question, a proposal, more delegation) is in the
// report's openQuestions and the task is not failed; its prose so far streams as message_progress
// events carrying its taskId (run-event.json). When it cannot finish (agent#17): at its time
// limit, what it had written, marked partial; one retry of a transient refusal before its first
// answer byte (reused, retried). What it cost (agent#18): tokens, firstByteMs and durationMs
// beside modelRequests, toolCalls and model, and the batch's figures in the parent's checkpoint
// (checkpoint.json delegation, provenance.json $defs/delegationReport).
